  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Energy Efficiency in AgriFood Cold Chain Logistic in China</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;Overall Objective: To enhance the resource-efficiency and sustainability of AgriFood Cold Chain Logistic in Tibet, Jingjinji and Shandong (China) by providing MSMEs/SMEs involved in Cold Chain Logistic with mechanisms to reduce energy use &amp;amp; GHG emissions of Logistic Services. Specific Objectives: SO1 &#xbf; Improve energy-efficiency of MSMEs/SMEs of Tibet, Jingjinji and Shandong involved in AgriFood Cold Chain Logistic Operations and Management (Logistic Services Providers and AgriFood Companies) through tools and capacity building enabling to evaluate, declare &amp;amp; improve the energy consumption and GHG emissions of their logistic services. SO2 &#xbf;Increase the market pull of low-carbon AgriFood Cold Chain Logistic Services in Tibet, Jingjinji and Shandong by creating the confidence and recognition of clients through standard/labelling programmes that demonstrate their commitment towards low-carbon services. SO3 &#xbf; Stimulate the development of Green Financing Landscape in Tibet, Jingjinji and Shandong by increasing knowledge of MSMEs/SMEs and Financial Institutions on the potential of energy-efficiency measures &amp;amp; green investments opportunities and by supporting them to access to green investments. SO4 &#xbf; Increase Chinese adoption of resource-efficiency Practices in AgriFood Cold Chain Logistic by means of up-scale/replication measures in further areas and activity sectors of China&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
